# 
_pdbx_database_remark.id     400 
_pdbx_database_remark.text   
;COMPOUND
The crystallographic asymmetric unit of insulin 
consists of two insulin monomers each consisting 
of two heterochains. 
The entry presents coordinates for monomer 1 
(chain indicators A and B) and monomer 2 (chain 
indicators C and D). There are two zinc ions per 
insulin hexamer located on the three-fold axis. 
The conformations of two monomers are different 
as the result of a change in conformation of the 
first eight residues of the B-chain.
;
